===== BUG-032 structural audit (single-tree, audited RTL only) =====

----- 1. the register the tree defines -----
  PASS: sha256_reg.rdl declares the DIGEST field with a hardware clear, so a clear strobe is expected
  PASS: the DIGEST window is software-readable only, so its value is produced entirely by hardware
  PASS: the window is eight dwords wide, the full SHA-256 result

----- 2. the two strobes the module forms -----
  PASS: the first strobe is ZEROIZE OR switch: asserted only when cleanup is actually requested
  PASS: the second strobe is NOT(NOT ZEROIZE AND switch), which reduces to ZEROIZE OR NOT switch
  PASS: zeroize_reg2 appears exactly three times: its declaration, this assignment and a single use

----- 3. where each strobe is consumed -----
  PASS: the DIGEST window's hardware clear is the sole consumer of the second strobe
  PASS: the BLOCK window beside it clears from the first strobe, so the two windows disagree
  PASS: the internal digest_reg is also cleared from the first strobe, so the register file is the outlier
  PASS: no write-enable suppression guards the DIGEST window, so the clear strobe alone decides its value

----- 4. the direction of the error (this is what sets severity) -----
  PASS: the generated register block gives hwclr priority over the unconditional hardware write
  PASS: caliptra_top builds the switch input from edge-detected transitions
  PASS: those transitions are single-cycle pulses, so the switch is low throughout normal operation
  PASS: the debug-lock term is likewise a transition, not a level

----- 5. what that means at the register interface -----
  PASS: STATUS.VALID still reports a completed hash, so software is told to read a window that is held at zero
  PASS: the window's hardware-write source is the live digest, which the priority clear overrides

